    <article class='prose prose-lg md:prose-xl dark:prose-invert min-w-full py-4'>
        <h1>About GetFOSS</h1>

        <p>
            GetFOSS is an independent blog about free and open-source software. Our goal is simple: help you
            find the best free software for any task — and know exactly what you are getting before you
            install it. No hype, no marketing fluff, no "top 50 apps" lists copied from each other. Just
            clear, honest guides to programs that respect you and your computer.
        </p>

        <h2>What We Cover</h2>
        <p>
            We write about open-source software for every part of your digital life: operating systems and
            Linux distros, office and productivity tools, graphics and design, photo, video, and audio
            editing, media players, development tools, security and privacy utilities, communication and
            email apps, internet and networking software, system utilities, and programs for education and
            science. If a category exists, chances are there is a great free alternative to a paid product —
            and our job is to find it and explain it.
        </p>

        <h2>How We Write</h2>
        <p>
            Every review on GetFOSS follows the same honest structure. We describe what the software does
            today — with the current version and its release date. We list its main features and
            capabilities, show which platforms it runs on, and give both sides: real advantages and real
            disadvantages, including the ones that might make it a bad choice for you. Each article ends
            with a straightforward verdict and links to the official project website and its official
            download page — nowhere else. Every guide carries a "Last updated" date, so you always know how
            fresh the information is.
        </p>

        <h2>Why Free and Open Source</h2>
        <p>
            Free and open-source software gives you four essential freedoms: to run the program for any
            purpose, to study how it works, to modify it, and to share it with others. In practice this
            means software that is transparent — anyone can inspect the code — which naturally leads to
            better privacy and security, faster fixes, and no lock-in, ads, or subscriptions. It is software
            built by communities, not by marketing departments. We believe most people would choose it more
            often if someone showed them where to start. That is what GetFOSS is for.
        </p>

        <h2>Independence</h2>
        <p>
            GetFOSS has no ads, no sponsorships, and no paid placements. We are not affiliated with any of
            the projects we cover, and no one can buy a place in our articles. The only opinion expressed
            here is ours.
        </p>

